title: t/system.t events subtest fails against a live daemon
updated: 2026-08-24T03:07:56Z
---

The events subtest asserts ref eq ARRAY outside its is_live() guard. A real daemon (verified against the rootless Podman socket at unix:///run/user/1000/podman/podman.sock) returns an empty body for a window with no events, _request returns undef, and ref undef is the empty string. Fix is a gated assertion: keep the ARRAY check for the mock, and assert only "no exception, and an arrayref or undef" live. Reproduce: API_DOCKER_TEST_HOST=unix:///run/user/1000/podman/podman.sock prove -lv t/system.t
